AWS-016 — Workflow Distribution

Document ID: AWS-016
Title: Workflow Distribution
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the Canonical Workflow Distribution Model (CWDM) for the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Canonical Workflow Distribution Model establishes the principles, architecture, governance, integrity mechanisms, and operational processes required to securely distribute Workflow Definitions, Workflow Programs, Workflow Interfaces, Workflow Packages, and related execution artifacts throughout the Atlas ecosystem.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Workflow distribution architecture
Distribution repositories
Distribution channels
Distribution packages
Synchronization
Integrity verification
Update strategies
Distribution governance

This specification applies to every governed distribution of workflow artifacts.

3. Canonical Definition

Workflow Distribution is the governed process of securely delivering Workflow Definitions and related execution artifacts from authoritative repositories to authorized Atlas environments while preserving integrity, authenticity, compatibility, traceability, and execution reproducibility.

Workflow Distribution moves workflow artifacts.

It SHALL NOT modify workflow semantics.

4. Objectives

The Workflow Distribution Model SHALL:

Preserve workflow integrity.
Enable trusted deployment.
Support reproducible execution.
Enable federation.
Support offline deployment.
Preserve governance.
Enable synchronization.
Support scalable engineering execution.
5. Distribution Principles

Every workflow distribution SHALL satisfy the following principles.

Authenticity

Every distributed workflow artifact SHALL originate from an authorized source.

Integrity

Workflow artifacts SHALL be verified before activation.

Version Consistency

Distributed workflows SHALL preserve declared version identifiers.

Traceability

Every workflow distribution SHALL remain permanently traceable.

Repeatability

Equivalent distribution requests SHALL produce equivalent workflow artifact sets.

Governance

Workflow distribution SHALL comply with applicable Canonical Policy Objects.

