7. Distribution Artifacts

Atlas recognizes the following distributable artifacts.

Artifact	Description
Workflow Definition	Executable workflow blueprint
Workflow Interface	Interaction contract
Workflow Package	Deployable workflow collection
Workflow Program	Coordinated execution system
Workflow Template	Reusable execution template
Distribution Manifest	Distribution metadata

Artifacts SHALL remain independently versioned.

8. Distribution Repositories

Atlas supports multiple repository types.

Repository	Purpose
Central Repository	Authoritative Atlas workflows
Organization Repository	Enterprise workflows
Domain Repository	Discipline-specific workflows
Project Repository	Project workflows
Offline Repository	Disconnected environments

Repositories SHALL expose immutable artifact identifiers.

9. Distribution Channels

Workflow distribution MAY occur through:

Secure API
Repository synchronization
Package transfer
Scheduled deployment
Event-driven deployment
Offline media

Distribution channels SHALL preserve authenticity and integrity.

10. Workflow Packages

Workflow Packages SHALL define:

Package identifier
Included workflow definitions
Workflow interfaces
Version manifest
Dependency manifest
Policy baseline requirements
Integrity metadata
Digital signatures

Packages SHALL remain immutable after publication.

11. Synchronization

Synchronization SHALL support:

Incremental updates
Full synchronization
Offline synchronization
Bidirectional federation
Conflict detection
Version reconciliation

Synchronization SHALL NOT overwrite active governed workflow definitions without authorization.

12. Integrity Verification

Every distributed artifact SHALL be verified for:

Digital signature
Artifact checksum
Version compatibility
Dependency completeness
Manifest integrity
Trust chain validity

Verification SHALL precede activation.

13. Update Strategies

Atlas supports the following update strategies.

Strategy	Description
Immediate	Deploy immediately
Scheduled	Deploy at defined time
Manual	Administrator initiated
Phased	Incremental rollout
Canary	Limited deployment before wider release
Emergency	Governed expedited deployment

The selected strategy SHALL be explicitly declared.

14. Distribution Lifecycle

Every workflow distribution SHALL support:

Prepared
